&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49185993</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 17:23:44 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Ask HN: What would make you list your AI product on a new marketplace?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49185927</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Right now the AI tool that wins is the one with the biggest marketing budget and hype, not the one that works best.&lt;p&gt;We want a marketplace where sellers have to show proof, so buyers can tell the difference before they pay. We are trying to bring proof and quality to the AI market.&lt;p&gt;We are building it now. It is not open yet, and before we go further we want to know what would actually make someone list on it.&lt;p&gt;If you sell an AI tool: what has gone wrong for you on existing marketplaces and directories? What would make you list on a new one, and what would make you walk away?&lt;p&gt;While building it we made two free tools, no signup.&lt;p&gt;The Achboard reads any AI product's website like a sceptical buyer would.&lt;p&gt;Comparima shows a product next to its closest alternatives with what each costs.&lt;p&gt;Both at achrima.com&lt;/p&gt;
